-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), lines 1 to 339 (regs 1 to 18) -- THE SEAT LAYER of piece er1.
-- Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30; not verified against the official text.
--
-- SEAT: a person who has lost work, or cannot work because of sickness, pregnancy, caring for a child or a family member, or who is
-- self-employed or a fisher, asking whether they qualify for Employment Insurance benefits, how many hours or weeks they need, how
-- much they would receive and for how long, and what they must do or tell the Commission. Nothing here is new law: every question
-- calls a rule of the layer-1 modules imported above and builds their records from plain inputs.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Each question takes one input per fact the person can state (yes/no, a number, a date, or a choice from the modules'
-- own lists), with an @desc worded as the person would be asked. Where a regulation fixes a number for the person (hours, an
-- amount of earnings, a rate), the answer is a number and a "not decided by this regulation" case is NOTHING, which the form shows
-- as no answer. Judgments the text hands to someone else (the Minister of National Revenue's figure of hours in reg 10(3); whether
-- an agreed number of hours is reasonable) are asked as facts, "if ... says". A fact that another provision of the Act decides (for
-- instance "would be insurable employment but for paragraph 5(2)(c)") is asked as a yes/no the person can answer from that provision.
--
-- HOHFELD. The Regulations give the person claims, powers and liabilities against the Commission, the employer, the Minister of
-- National Revenue and Statistics Canada; each question takes the other party's side of the relation as inputs (who agreed, who
-- consented, what the employer can show, what the Commission referred the person to). NOTES.md "Jural relations" lists them.
--
-- GROUPING. The `§` headings follow the Regulations' order. A group that arises only in a situation the person may not be in says so
-- in its comment, so the form can ask "Has this happened to you?" first.
--
-- No seat is written for an official. Provisions that state only a duty of the Commission with no consequence for the person
-- (reg 18(2), the review of regional boundaries; reg 1(1) "pay period", used by other provisions) are encoded in layer 1 and have no question.

§ `Employment Insurance Regulations -- the questions of a person asking about benefits (regulations 1 to 18)`

§§ `Regulation 1 -- who is a family member, a guardian, critically ill, and what care and support are`

-- Situation: you are caring for, or supporting, someone who is ill or injured, or you are asking about a medical certificate (the
-- form can ask "Are you looking after someone who is ill or injured?" before showing this group).

-- reg 1(3) "family member". The seventeen kinds are independent: answer yes to every one that fits. The words ward and guardian
-- are defined in reg 1(4) (the next two questions).
@export Is the person I care for or support my family member under regulation 1(3)?
GIVEN `they are my spouse or common-law partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they your spouse or common-law partner?
      `they are my child or the child of my spouse or common-law partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they your child, or the child of your spouse or common-law partner?
      `they are my parent or the spouse or common-law partner of my parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they your parent, or the spouse or common-law partner of your parent?
      `they are a child of my parent or of my parent's spouse or common-law partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they a child of your parent, or a child of the spouse or common-law partner of your parent (a brother, sister, half-brother or half-sister)?
      `they are a grandparent of mine or of my spouse or common-law partner, or the spouse or common-law partner of a grandparent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they a grandparent of you or of your spouse or common-law partner, or the spouse or common-law partner of your grandparent?
      `they are a grandchild of mine or of my spouse or common-law partner, or the spouse or common-law partner of a grandchild` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they a grandchild of you or of your spouse or common-law partner, or the spouse or common-law partner of your grandchild?
      `they are the spouse or common-law partner of my child or of the child of my spouse or common-law partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they the spouse or common-law partner of your child, or of the child of your spouse or common-law partner?
      `they are a parent, or the spouse or common-law partner of a parent, of my spouse or common-law partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they a parent of your spouse or common-law partner, or the spouse or common-law partner of that parent?
      `they are the spouse or common-law partner of a child of my parent or of the child of my parent's spouse or common-law partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they the spouse or common-law partner of a child of your parent, or of a child of your parent's spouse or common-law partner?
      `they are a child of a parent of my spouse or common-law partner or of that parent's spouse or common-law partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they a child of a parent of your spouse or common-law partner, or a child of the spouse or common-law partner of that parent?
      `they are an uncle or aunt of mine or of my spouse or common-law partner, or the spouse or common-law partner of an uncle or aunt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they an uncle or aunt of you or of your spouse or common-law partner, or the spouse or common-law partner of your uncle or aunt?
      `they are a nephew or niece of mine or of my spouse or common-law partner, or the spouse or common-law partner of a nephew or niece` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they a nephew or niece of you or of your spouse or common-law partner, or the spouse or common-law partner of your nephew or niece?
      `they are, or were, a foster parent of me or of my spouse or common-law partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they, or were they, a foster parent of you or of your spouse or common-law partner?
      `they are, or were, a foster child of me or of my spouse or common-law partner, or the spouse or common-law partner of that child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they, or were they, a foster child of you or of your spouse or common-law partner, or the spouse or common-law partner of that child?
      `they are, or were, a ward of me or of my spouse or common-law partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they, or were they, a ward of you or of your spouse or common-law partner (a ward is a person for whom a guardian is appointed)?
      `they are, or were, a guardian of me or the spouse or common-law partner of that guardian` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they, or were they, your guardian, or the spouse or common-law partner of your guardian?
      `I consider them to be like a close relative or they consider me to be` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether or not you are related by marriage, common-law partnership or a legal parent-child relationship, do you consider them to be like a close relative, or do they consider you to be?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the person I care for or support my family member under regulation 1(3)` IF
    `reg 1(3) family member` `the relationship I have to them`
    WHERE
        `the relationship I have to them` MEANS `er1 Relationship to an individual` WITH
            `er1 (a) the spouse or common-law partner of the individual` IS `they are my spouse or common-law partner`
            `er1 (b) a child of the individual or a child of the individual's spouse or common-law partner` IS `they are my child or the child of my spouse or common-law partner`
            `er1 (c) a parent of the individual or a spouse or common-law partner of the parent` IS `they are my parent or the spouse or common-law partner of my parent`
            `er1 (d) a child of the individual's parent or a child of the spouse or common-law partner of the individual's parent` IS `they are a child of my parent or of my parent's spouse or common-law partner`
            `er1 (e) a grandparent of the individual or of the individual's spouse or common-law partner or the spouse or common-law partner of the individual's grandparent` IS `they are a grandparent of mine or of my spouse or common-law partner, or the spouse or common-law partner of a grandparent`
            `er1 (f) a grandchild of the individual or of the individual's spouse or common-law partner or the spouse or common-law partner of the individual's grandchild` IS `they are a grandchild of mine or of my spouse or common-law partner, or the spouse or common-law partner of a grandchild`
            `er1 (g) the spouse or common-law partner of the individual's child or of the child of the individual's spouse or common-law partner` IS `they are the spouse or common-law partner of my child or of the child of my spouse or common-law partner`
            `er1 (h) a parent, or the spouse or common-law partner of a parent, of the individual's spouse or common-law partner` IS `they are a parent, or the spouse or common-law partner of a parent, of my spouse or common-law partner`
            `er1 (i) the spouse or common-law partner of a child of the individual's parent or of a child of the spouse or common-law partner of the individual's parent` IS `they are the spouse or common-law partner of a child of my parent or of the child of my parent's spouse or common-law partner`
            `er1 (j) a child of a parent of the individual's spouse or common-law partner or a child of the spouse or common-law partner of the parent of the individual's spouse or common-law partner` IS `they are a child of a parent of my spouse or common-law partner or of that parent's spouse or common-law partner`
            `er1 (k) an uncle or aunt of the individual or of the individual's spouse or common-law partner or the spouse or common-law partner of the individual's uncle or aunt` IS `they are an uncle or aunt of mine or of my spouse or common-law partner, or the spouse or common-law partner of an uncle or aunt`
            `er1 (l) a nephew or niece of the individual or of the individual's spouse or common-law partner or the spouse or common-law partner of the individual's nephew or niece` IS `they are a nephew or niece of mine or of my spouse or common-law partner, or the spouse or common-law partner of a nephew or niece`
            `er1 (m) a current or former foster parent of the individual or of the individual's spouse or common-law partner` IS `they are, or were, a foster parent of me or of my spouse or common-law partner`
            `er1 (n) a current or former foster child of the individual or the spouse or common-law partner of that child` IS `they are, or were, a foster child of me or of my spouse or common-law partner, or the spouse or common-law partner of that child`
            `er1 (o) a current or former ward of the individual or of the individual's spouse or common-law partner` IS `they are, or were, a ward of me or of my spouse or common-law partner`
            `er1 (p) a current or former guardian of the individual or the spouse or common-law partner of that guardian` IS `they are, or were, a guardian of me or the spouse or common-law partner of that guardian`
            `er1 (q) a person whom the individual considers to be like a close relative or who considers the individual to be like a close relative` IS `I consider them to be like a close relative or they consider me to be`

-- reg 1(4) "guardian".
@export Is this person a guardian under regulation 1(4)?
GIVEN `they are legally authorized to act on behalf of a minor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they legally authorized to act on behalf of a minor?
      `they are legally authorized to act on behalf of an incapable adult` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they legally authorized to act on behalf of an adult who cannot manage for themselves?
      `they are a tutor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they a tutor?
      `they are a curator` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they a curator?
      `they are a mandatary acting under a protection mandate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they a mandatary acting under a protection mandate?
      `they are appointed to act in a similar capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they appointed to act in a capacity similar to a guardian, tutor, curator or mandatary?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this person a guardian under regulation 1(4)` IF
    `reg 1(4) guardian`
        `they are legally authorized to act on behalf of a minor`
        `they are legally authorized to act on behalf of an incapable adult`
        `they are a tutor`
        `they are a curator`
        `they are a mandatary acting under a protection mandate`
        `they are appointed to act in a similar capacity`

-- reg 1(4) "ward".
@export Is this person my ward under regulation 1(4)?
GIVEN `a guardian is appointed for them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a guardian appointed for them?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this person my ward under regulation 1(4)` IF
    `reg 1(4) ward` `a guardian is appointed for them`

-- reg 1(5) "care".
@export Does the help I give count as care under regulation 1(5)?
GIVEN `the person I help is a family member, a critically ill child or a critically ill adult` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person you help a family member of the kind described in subsection 23.1(2) or 152.06(1) of the Act, a critically ill child or a critically ill adult?
      `the help is required because of the state of health of that person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the help required because of the state of health of that person?
      `the help is provided by a health care professional` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the help provided by a health care professional?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the help I give count as care under regulation 1(5)` IF
    `reg 1(5) care` `the person I help is a family member, a critically ill child or a critically ill adult` `the help is required because of the state of health of that person` `the help is provided by a health care professional`

-- reg 1(5) "support".
@export Does the help I give count as support under regulation 1(5)?
GIVEN `the person I help is a family member, a critically ill child or a critically ill adult` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person you help a family member of the kind described in subsection 23.1(2) or 152.06(1) of the Act, a critically ill child or a critically ill adult?
      `the psychological or emotional support is required because of the state of health of that person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the psychological or emotional support required because of the state of health of that person?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the help I give count as support under regulation 1(5)` IF
    `reg 1(5) support` `the person I help is a family member, a critically ill child or a critically ill adult` `the psychological or emotional support is required because of the state of health of that person`

-- reg 1(6) "critically ill child".
@export Is the child I am caring for a critically ill child under regulation 1(6)?
GIVEN `the child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is the child's date of birth?
      `the day on which the period referred to in subsection 23.2(3) or 152.061(3) of the Act begins` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the period referred to in subsection 23.2(3) or 152.061(3) of the Act begin (the Commission or the certificate tells you)?
      `the child's baseline state of health has significantly changed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the child's baseline state of health significantly changed?
      `the child's life is at risk as a result of an illness or injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child's life at risk as a result of an illness or injury?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the child I am caring for a critically ill child under regulation 1(6)` IF
    `reg 1(6) critically ill child`
        `the child's date of birth`
        `the day on which the period referred to in subsection 23.2(3) or 152.061(3) of the Act begins`
        `the child's baseline state of health has significantly changed`
        `the child's life is at risk as a result of an illness or injury`

-- reg 1(7) "critically ill adult".
@export Is the adult I am caring for a critically ill adult under regulation 1(7)?
GIVEN `the adult's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is the adult's date of birth?
      `the day on which the period referred to in subsection 23.3(3) or 152.062(3) of the Act begins` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the period referred to in subsection 23.3(3) or 152.062(3) of the Act begin (the Commission or the certificate tells you)?
      `the adult's baseline state of health has significantly changed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the adult's baseline state of health significantly changed?
      `the adult's life is at risk as a result of an illness or injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the adult's life at risk as a result of an illness or injury?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the adult I am caring for a critically ill adult under regulation 1(7)` IF
    `reg 1(7) critically ill adult`
        `the adult's date of birth`
        `the day on which the period referred to in subsection 23.3(3) or 152.062(3) of the Act begins`
        `the adult's baseline state of health has significantly changed`
        `the adult's life is at risk as a result of an illness or injury`

-- reg 1(3) "nurse practitioner": for a medical certificate (the Act and Regulations elsewhere ask for one).
@export Is my health practitioner a nurse practitioner under regulation 1(3)?
GIVEN `they are a registered nurse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they a registered nurse?
      `they are entitled under the laws of a province to practise as a nurse practitioner or under an equivalent designation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they entitled under the laws of a province to practise as a nurse practitioner, or under an equivalent title?
      `they are entitled to autonomously make diagnoses` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they entitled to make diagnoses on their own?
      `they are entitled to autonomously order and interpret diagnostic tests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they entitled to order and interpret diagnostic tests on their own?
      `they are entitled to autonomously prescribe substances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they entitled to prescribe substances on their own?
      `they are entitled to autonomously treat patients` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they entitled to treat patients on their own?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my health practitioner a nurse practitioner under regulation 1(3)` IF
    `reg 1(3) nurse practitioner`
        `they are a registered nurse`
        `they are entitled under the laws of a province to practise as a nurse practitioner or under an equivalent designation`
        `they are entitled to autonomously make diagnoses`
        `they are entitled to autonomously order and interpret diagnostic tests`
        `they are entitled to autonomously prescribe substances`
        `they are entitled to autonomously treat patients`

-- reg 1(2) "international organization": relevant if you work for an organization of that kind (see regulation 3).
@export Is my employer an international organization under regulation 1(2)?
GIVEN `my employer is a specialized agency of which Canada is a member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employer a specialized agency of which Canada is a member?
      `it is brought into relationship with the United Nations in accordance with article 63 of the Charter of the United Nations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it brought into relationship with the United Nations in accordance with article 63 of the Charter of the United Nations?
      `my employer is an international organization of which Canada is a member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employer an international organization of which Canada is a member?
      `its primary purpose is the maintenance of international peace` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is its primary purpose the maintenance of international peace?
      `its primary purpose is the economic or social well-being of a community of nations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is its primary purpose the economic or social well-being of a community of nations?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my employer an international organization under regulation 1(2)` IF
    `reg 1(2) international organization`
        `my employer is a specialized agency of which Canada is a member`
        `it is brought into relationship with the United Nations in accordance with article 63 of the Charter of the United Nations`
        `my employer is an international organization of which Canada is a member`
        `its primary purpose is the maintenance of international peace`
        `its primary purpose is the economic or social well-being of a community of nations`

§§ `Regulations 2 to 6 -- does the Regulation make my work insurable employment`

-- Situation: your work is for a provincial or foreign government, an international organization, on a ship, or outside Canada, or is
-- one of the kinds of work reg 6 names (the form can ask "Is your work any of these?" first). Whether work counts as insurable employment
-- at all is section 5 of the Act (the core); these questions answer only what the Regulations add.

@export Is my work for a provincial government included in insurable employment under regulation 2?
GIVEN `my work is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your work done in Canada?
      `I am appointed under an Act governing the province's public service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you appointed under an Act governing the province's public service?
      `I am remunerated under an Act governing the province's public service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you remunerated under an Act governing the province's public service?
      `I am employed in Canada by an agent of the province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you work in Canada for a corporation, commission or other body that is an agent of the province?
      `my work would be insurable employment but for paragraph 5(2)(c) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would your work be insurable employment if paragraph 5(2)(c) of the Act (employment by a province) did not exclude it?
      `the province's government has entered into an agreement with the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the province's government entered into an agreement with the Commission?
      `the agreement waives the exclusion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement say that the province's government waives the exclusion?
      `the agreement insures all its employees engaged in such employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement say that the province's government will insure all its employees engaged in such employment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my work for a provincial government included in insurable employment under regulation 2` IF
    `reg 2(1) employment in Canada by Her Majesty in right of a province`
        `my work is in Canada`
        `I am appointed under an Act governing the province's public service`
        `I am remunerated under an Act governing the province's public service`
        `I am employed in Canada by an agent of the province`
        `my work would be insurable employment but for paragraph 5(2)(c) of the Act`
        `the province's government has entered into an agreement with the Commission`
        `the agreement waives the exclusion`
        `the agreement insures all its employees engaged in such employment`

@export Is my work for a foreign government or an international organization included in insurable employment under regulation 3?
GIVEN `my work is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your work done in Canada?
      `my employer is the government of another country or of one of its political subdivisions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employer the government of a country other than Canada, or of a political subdivision of that country?
      `my employer is an international organization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employer an international organization (see the question on regulation 1(2))?
      `my work would be insurable employment but for paragraphs 5(2)(d) and (e) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would your work be insurable employment if paragraphs 5(2)(d) and (e) of the Act (employment by a foreign government or an international organization) did not exclude it?
      `my employer consents in writing to the inclusion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your employer (the government or the international organization) consented in writing to the inclusion of your work in insurable employment?
      `a consent was given under the Unemployment Insurance Regulations as they read immediately before June 30, 1996` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a consent given under the Unemployment Insurance Regulations, as they read immediately before June 30, 1996?
      `that consent has been revoked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has that consent been revoked?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my work for a foreign government or an international organization included in insurable employment under regulation 3` IF
    `reg 3(1) employment by a foreign government or an international organization`
        `my work is in Canada`
        `my employer is the government of another country or of one of its political subdivisions`
        `my employer is an international organization`
        `my work would be insurable employment but for paragraphs 5(2)(d) and (e) of the Act`
        `my employer consents in writing to the inclusion`
        (`reg 3(2) the consent is considered to be a consent referred to in subsection (1)` `a consent was given under the Unemployment Insurance Regulations as they read immediately before June 30, 1996` `that consent has been revoked`)

@export Is my work on a ship outside Canada included in insurable employment under regulation 4?
GIVEN `my work is on a ship outside Canada or partly outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your work on a ship outside Canada or partly outside Canada?
      `my work would be insurable employment if it were in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would your work be insurable employment if it were in Canada?
      `the ship is of Canadian registry or licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the ship of Canadian registry or licence?
      `the ship is regularly employed in voyages between ports outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the ship regularly employed in voyages between ports outside Canada?
      `the ship has been chartered to a person resident outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the ship been chartered to a person resident outside Canada?
      `the ship has been chartered to a person resident in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the ship been chartered to a person resident in Canada?
      `the ship is regularly employed in voyages from a port in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the ship regularly employed in voyages from a port in Canada?
      `the operation of the ship is principally controlled in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the operation of the ship principally controlled in Canada?
      `the owner or managing owner of the ship resides or has a place of business in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the owner or managing owner of the ship reside or have a place of business in Canada?
      `an agreement between Canada and the ship's jurisdiction makes employment on it subject to the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is any employment on the ship subject to the Employment Insurance Act by an agreement between the Government of Canada and the government of the jurisdiction in which the ship is registered?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my work on a ship outside Canada included in insurable employment under regulation 4` IF
    `reg 4 employment on a ship outside Canada`
        `my work is on a ship outside Canada or partly outside Canada`
        `my work would be insurable employment if it were in Canada`
        `the ship is of Canadian registry or licence`
        `the ship is regularly employed in voyages between ports outside Canada`
        `the ship has been chartered to a person resident outside Canada`
        `the ship has been chartered to a person resident in Canada`
        `the ship is regularly employed in voyages from a port in Canada`
        `the operation of the ship is principally controlled in Canada`
        `the owner or managing owner of the ship resides or has a place of business in Canada`
        `an agreement between Canada and the ship's jurisdiction makes employment on it subject to the Act`

@export Is my work outside Canada included in insurable employment under regulation 5?
GIVEN `my work is outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your work done outside Canada?
      `my work is on a ship described in regulation 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your work on a ship of the kind regulation 4 describes (a ship outside or partly outside Canada)?
      `I ordinarily reside in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you ordinarily reside in Canada?
      `my employer is resident or has a place of business in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employer resident in Canada, or does it have a place of business in Canada?
      `my work would be insurable employment if it were in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would your work be insurable employment if it were in Canada?
      `my work is not insurable employment under the laws of the country where it takes place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your work not insurable employment under the laws of the country where it takes place?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my work outside Canada included in insurable employment under regulation 5` IF
    `reg 5 employment outside Canada`
        `my work is outside Canada`
        `my work is on a ship described in regulation 4`
        `I ordinarily reside in Canada`
        `my employer is resident or has a place of business in Canada`
        `my work would be insurable employment if it were in Canada`
        `my work is not insurable employment under the laws of the country where it takes place`

-- Regulation 6: seven kinds of work. Each question asks one kind; "unless it is excluded" is the last input of each (regulations 7 to 9
-- and any other provision of the Regulations: see the questions that follow). The other six kinds are passed as "not this kind" because
-- the question is about the kind asked.

@export Is my work for my union included in insurable employment under regulation 6(a)?
GIVEN `I am a union member employed by my union` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a union member employed by your own union?
      `my work is conducting union business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your work conducting union business?
      `my work is picketing in a labour dispute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your work picketing in a labour dispute?
      `a provision of these Regulations excludes my work from insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a provision of the Employment Insurance Regulations (regulations 7 to 9, for instance) exclude your work from insurable employment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my work for my union included in insurable employment under regulation 6(a)` IF
    `reg 6 employment included`
        (`reg 6(a) employment of a union member by the member's union` `I am a union member employed by my union` `my work is conducting union business` `my work is picketing in a labour dispute`)
        FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
        `a provision of these Regulations excludes my work from insurable employment`

@export Is my work as an apprentice or trainee included in insurable employment under regulation 6(b)?
GIVEN `I am employed as an apprentice or trainee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed as an apprentice or trainee (even if you do not perform any services for your employer)?
      `a provision of these Regulations excludes my work from insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a provision of the Employment Insurance Regulations (regulations 7 to 9, for instance) exclude your work from insurable employment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my work as an apprentice or trainee included in insurable employment under regulation 6(b)` IF
    `reg 6 employment included`
        FALSE
        (`reg 6(b) employment of a person as an apprentice or trainee` `I am employed as an apprentice or trainee`)
        FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
        `a provision of these Regulations excludes my work from insurable employment`

@export Is my work as a member of the clergy or of a religious order included in insurable employment under regulation 6(c)?
GIVEN `I am employed as a member of the clergy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed as a member of the clergy?
      `I am employed as a member of a religious order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed as a member of a religious order?
      `a provision of these Regulations excludes my work from insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a provision of the Employment Insurance Regulations (regulations 7 to 9, for instance) exclude your work from insurable employment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my work as a member of the clergy or of a religious order included in insurable employment under regulation 6(c)` IF
    `reg 6 employment included`
        FALSE FALSE
        (`reg 6(c) employment of a person as a member of the clergy or of a religious order` `I am employed as a member of the clergy` `I am employed as a member of a religious order`)
        FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
        `a provision of these Regulations excludes my work from insurable employment`

@export Is my work in a barbering or hairdressing establishment included in insurable employment under regulation 6(d)?
GIVEN `I am employed in a barbering or hairdressing establishment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed in a barbering or hairdressing establishment?
      `I provide services normally provided in such an establishment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you provide any of the services that are normally provided in such an establishment?
      `I am the owner or operator of the establishment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the owner or operator of the establishment?
      `a provision of these Regulations excludes my work from insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a provision of the Employment Insurance Regulations (regulations 7 to 9, for instance) exclude your work from insurable employment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my work in a barbering or hairdressing establishment included in insurable employment under regulation 6(d)` IF
    `reg 6 employment included`
        FALSE FALSE FALSE
        (`reg 6(d) employment in a barbering or hairdressing establishment` `I am employed in a barbering or hairdressing establishment` `I provide services normally provided in such an establishment` `I am the owner or operator of the establishment`)
        FALSE FALSE FALSE
        `a provision of these Regulations excludes my work from insurable employment`

@export Is my work as a driver of a passenger vehicle included in insurable employment under regulation 6(e)?
GIVEN `I am employed as a driver of a vehicle that carries passengers for a business or public authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed as the driver of a taxi, commercial bus, school bus or other vehicle used by a business or public authority to carry passengers?
      `the portion of the vehicle that I own` IS A NUMBER @desc What portion of the vehicle do you own? (a fraction: 0 if none, 0.5 for half, 1 if all)
      `I am the owner or operator of the business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the owner or operator of the business?
      `I am the operator of the public authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the operator of the public authority?
      `a provision of these Regulations excludes my work from insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a provision of the Employment Insurance Regulations (regulations 7 to 9, for instance) exclude your work from insurable employment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my work as a driver of a passenger vehicle included in insurable employment under regulation 6(e)` IF
    `reg 6 employment included`
        FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
        (`reg 6(e) employment as a driver of a vehicle that carries passengers` `I am employed as a driver of a vehicle that carries passengers for a business or public authority` `the portion of the vehicle that I own` `I am the owner or operator of the business` `I am the operator of the public authority`)
        FALSE FALSE
        `a provision of these Regulations excludes my work from insurable employment`

@export Is my work as the holder of an office included in insurable employment under regulation 6(f)?
GIVEN `I hold an office as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Canada Pension Plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold an office as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Canada Pension Plan?
      `my office is in or under the federal public administration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your office in or under a department or other portion of the federal public administration set out in Schedule I, II, III, IV or V to the Financial Administration Act?
      `I am appointed and remunerated under an Act governing the public service of a province that has agreed to insure all its employees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you appointed and remunerated under an Act governing the public service of a province whose government has agreed (under regulation 2(1)) to insure all its employees?
      `I hold the office in or under an agent of such a province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold the office in or under a corporation, commission or other body that is an agent of such a province?
      `I hold the office in a union or an association of unions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold the office in a union or an association of unions?
      `I was elected to the office by popular vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you elected to the office by popular vote?
      `I was elected or appointed to the office in a representative capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you elected or appointed to the office in the union or association in a representative capacity?
      `regulation 6(a) already includes that work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your work already included in insurable employment by paragraph (a) of regulation 6 (work for your union conducting union business)?
      `a provision of these Regulations excludes my work from insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a provision of the Employment Insurance Regulations (regulations 7 to 9, for instance) exclude your work from insurable employment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my work as the holder of an office included in insurable employment under regulation 6(f)` IF
    `reg 6 employment included`
        FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
        (`reg 6(f) employment of a person who holds an office`
            `I hold an office as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Canada Pension Plan`
            `my office is in or under the federal public administration`
            `I am appointed and remunerated under an Act governing the public service of a province that has agreed to insure all its employees`
            `I hold the office in or under an agent of such a province`
            `I hold the office in a union or an association of unions`
            `I was elected to the office by popular vote`
            `I was elected or appointed to the office in a representative capacity`
            `regulation 6(a) already includes that work`)
        FALSE
        `a provision of these Regulations excludes my work from insurable employment`

@export Is my work placed by an agency included in insurable employment under regulation 6(g)?
GIVEN `a placement or employment agency placed me in the work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a placement or employment agency place you in the work?
      `I perform services for and under the direction and control of a client of the agency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you perform services for and under the direction and control of a client of the agency?
      `the agency pays me for those services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agency pay you for those services?
      `a provision of these Regulations excludes my work from insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a provision of the Employment Insurance Regulations (regulations 7 to 9, for instance) exclude your work from insurable employment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my work placed by an agency included in insurable employment under regulation 6(g)` IF
    `reg 6 employment included`
        FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
        (`reg 6(g) employment of a person who is placed by a placement or employment agency` `a placement or employment agency placed me in the work` `I perform services for and under the direction and control of a client of the agency` `the agency pays me for those services`)
        `a provision of these Regulations excludes my work from insurable employment`

§§ `Regulations 7 to 9 -- does the Regulation take my work out of insurable employment`

-- Situation: your work is for a religious order, for premiums paid abroad, a rescue operation, an employment support measure, a short job
-- (a fair, circus, election or referendum) or farm work (the form can ask "Is your work any of these?" first).

@export Is my work as a member of a religious order excluded from insurable employment under regulation 7(b)?
GIVEN `I am a member of a religious order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of a religious order?
      `I have taken a vow of poverty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you taken a vow of poverty?
      `my remuneration is paid directly to the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your remuneration paid directly to the order?
      `my remuneration is paid by me to the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you pay your remuneration to the order yourself?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my work as a member of a religious order excluded from insurable employment under regulation 7(b)` IF
    `reg 7(b) employment of a member of a religious order who has taken a vow of poverty`
        `I am a member of a religious order` `I have taken a vow of poverty` `my remuneration is paid directly to the order` `my remuneration is paid by me to the order`

@export Is my work excluded from insurable employment under regulation 7(c) because premiums are payable in the United States?
GIVEN `premiums are payable under the unemployment insurance law of a United States state, the District of Columbia, Puerto Rico or the Virgin Islands` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are premiums payable for your work under the unemployment insurance law of any state of the United States, the District of Columbia, Puerto Rico or the Virgin Islands?
      `that is by reason of the Canada-United States agreement of March 6 and 12, 1942` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that by reason of the Agreement between Canada and the United States Respecting Unemployment Insurance, signed on March 6 and 12, 1942?
      `premiums are payable under the Railroad Unemployment Insurance Act of the United States` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are premiums payable for your work under the Railroad Unemployment Insurance Act of the United States?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my work excluded from insurable employment under regulation 7(c) because premiums are payable in the United States` IF
    `reg 7(c) employment in respect of which premiums are payable under the law of the United States`
        `premiums are payable under the unemployment insurance law of a United States state, the District of Columbia, Puerto Rico or the Virgin Islands`
        `that is by reason of the Canada-United States agreement of March 6 and 12, 1942`
        `premiums are payable under the Railroad Unemployment Insurance Act of the United States`

@export Is my work in Canada excluded from insurable employment under regulation 7(d) because I live in another country?
GIVEN `my work is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your work done in Canada?
      `I reside in a country other than Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you reside in a country other than Canada?
      `premiums are payable for my services in Canada under the unemployment insurance laws of that other country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are premiums payable for your services in Canada under the unemployment insurance laws of that other country?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my work in Canada excluded from insurable employment under regulation 7(d) because I live in another country` IF
    `reg 7(d) employment in Canada of a person who resides in another country`
        `my work is in Canada` `I reside in a country other than Canada` `premiums are payable for my services in Canada under the unemployment insurance laws of that other country`

@export Is my work on a rescue operation excluded from insurable employment under regulation 7(e)?
GIVEN `my work is for the purpose of a rescue operation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your work for the purpose of a rescue operation?
      `I am regularly employed by the employer who employs me for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you regularly employed by the employer who employs you for that purpose?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my work on a rescue operation excluded from insurable employment under regulation 7(e)` IF
    `reg 7(e) employment for the purpose of a rescue operation`
        `my work is for the purpose of a rescue operation` `I am regularly employed by the employer who employs me for that purpose`

@export Is my work under an employment support measure excluded from insurable employment under regulation 7(f)?
GIVEN `my work is under an employment support measure referred to in paragraph 59(b) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your work under an employment support measure referred to in paragraph 59(b) of the Act?
      `my work is under a measure that is the subject of an agreement under section 63 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your work under a measure that is the subject of an agreement under section 63 of the Act?
      `the measure is established to help insured participants start businesses or become self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the measure established to help insured participants start businesses or become self-employed?
      `the measure is established to give insured participants work experience to improve their long-term employment prospects` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the measure established to provide insured participants with employment opportunities through which they can gain work experience to improve their long-term employment prospects?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my work under an employment support measure excluded from insurable employment under regulation 7(f)` IF
    `reg 7(f) employment under an employment support measure`
        `my work is under an employment support measure referred to in paragraph 59(b) of the Act`
        `my work is under a measure that is the subject of an agreement under section 63 of the Act`
        `the measure is established to help insured participants start businesses or become self-employed`
        `the measure is established to give insured participants work experience to improve their long-term employment prospects`

@export Is my short job at a circus, fair or similar activity excluded from insurable employment under regulation 8(1)(a)?
GIVEN `my job is in connection with a circus, fair, parade, carnival, exposition, exhibition or other similar activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your job in connection with a circus, fair, parade, carnival, exposition, exhibition or other similar activity?
      `I am employed as an entertainer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed as an entertainer?
      `I am regularly employed by that employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you regularly employed by that employer?
      `the number of days in the year that I am employed by that employer in that job` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days in the year are you employed by that employer in that job?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my short job at a circus, fair or similar activity excluded from insurable employment under regulation 8(1)(a)` IF
    `reg 8(1)(a) employment in connection with a circus, fair or similar activity`
        `my job is in connection with a circus, fair, parade, carnival, exposition, exhibition or other similar activity`
        `I am employed as an entertainer`
        `I am regularly employed by that employer`
        `the number of days in the year that I am employed by that employer in that job`

@export Is my short job for an election or referendum excluded from insurable employment under regulation 8(1)(c)?
GIVEN `my employer is the federal government, a provincial government, a municipality or a school board` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employer Her Majesty in right of Canada, the government of a province, a municipality or a school board?
      `my job is in connection with a referendum or election to public office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your job in connection with a referendum or an election to public office?
      `I am regularly employed by that employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you regularly employed by that employer?
      `the year of the job` IS A NUMBER @desc In which year did you do the job? (for example 2026)
      `the number of hours in the year that I am employed by that employer in that job` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many hours in that year are you employed by that employer in that job?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my short job for an election or referendum excluded from insurable employment under regulation 8(1)(c)` IF
    `reg 8(1)(c) employment in connection with a referendum or election`
        `my employer is the federal government, a provincial government, a municipality or a school board`
        `my job is in connection with a referendum or election to public office`
        `I am regularly employed by that employer`
        `the year of the job`
        `the number of hours in the year that I am employed by that employer in that job`

@export From when is my short job insurable once it becomes a regular employment under regulation 8(2)?
GIVEN `my job was excluded from insurable employment under regulation 8(1)(a) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your job excluded from insurable employment under paragraph (1)(a) or (c) of regulation 8?
      `my job became a regular employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your job become a regular employment?
      `the day on which it became a regular employment` IS A DATE @desc On what day did it become a regular employment?
      `the hour of that day, 0 to 23, at which it became a regular employment` IS A NUMBER @desc At what hour of that day (0 to 23) did it become a regular employment? (the hour matters for an election or referendum job; for a fair or circus job use 0)
GIVETH A MAYBE `er1 Day and hour`
DECIDE `From when is my short job insurable once it becomes a regular employment under regulation 8(2)` IS
    `reg 8(2) the point from which the employment is insurable`
        `my job was excluded from insurable employment under regulation 8(1)(a) or (c)`
        `my job became a regular employment`
        (`er1 Day and hour` OF `the day on which it became a regular employment`, `the hour of that day, 0 to 23, at which it became a regular employment`)

@export From which day are my short jobs for the same employer insurable together under regulation 8(3)?
GIVEN `I have been employed by the same employer in one or more jobs excluded under regulation 8(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been employed by the same employer in one or more jobs that regulation 8(1)(a) excludes from insurable employment?
      `the total number of days of those jobs in the same year` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days in total, in that year, did those jobs last?
      `the day on which the total period of employment began` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the total period of employment begin?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `From which day are my short jobs for the same employer insurable together under regulation 8(3)` IS
    `reg 8(3) the day from which the employments taken together are insurable`
        `I have been employed by the same employer in one or more jobs excluded under regulation 8(1)(a)`
        `the total number of days of those jobs in the same year`
        `the day on which the total period of employment began`

@export From which hour are my short election or referendum jobs for the same employer insurable together under regulation 8(4)?
GIVEN `I have been employed by the same employer in one or more jobs excluded under regulation 8(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been employed by the same employer in one or more jobs that regulation 8(1)(c) excludes from insurable employment?
      `the total number of hours of those jobs in the same year` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours in total, in that year, did those jobs last?
      `the day on which the total period of employment began` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the total period of employment begin?
      `the hour of that day, 0 to 23, at which the total period of employment began` IS A NUMBER @desc At what hour of that day (0 to 23) did the total period of employment begin?
GIVETH A MAYBE `er1 Day and hour`
DECIDE `From which hour are my short election or referendum jobs for the same employer insurable together under regulation 8(4)` IS
    `reg 8(4) the hour from which the employments taken together are insurable`
        `I have been employed by the same employer in one or more jobs excluded under regulation 8(1)(c)`
        `the total number of hours of those jobs in the same year`
        (`er1 Day and hour` OF `the day on which the total period of employment began`, `the hour of that day, 0 to 23, at which the total period of employment began`)

@export Is my farm work agriculture under regulation 9(1)?
GIVEN operation IS A `er1 Operation that the definition of agriculture lists` @desc Which of the listed farm operations is your work? Choose the one that fits, or the last choice if none of them does.
      `it is carried out on a farm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the work carried out on a farm?
      `the selling is incidental to the farm operations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your work is offering for sale or selling farm products: is that incidental to the farm operations that produced them?
      `the handling is incidental to the offering for sale or selling` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your work is exhibiting, advertising, assembling, freezing, storing, grading, preparing, processing, packing or transporting those products: is it incidental to offering them for sale or selling them?
      `it is operations of farming carried out for the benefit of a person who is a farmer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whatever the list says, is your work operations of farming carried out for the benefit of a person who is a farmer?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my farm work agriculture under regulation 9(1)` IF
    `reg 9(1) agriculture` operation `it is carried out on a farm` `the selling is incidental to the farm operations` `the handling is incidental to the offering for sale or selling` `it is operations of farming carried out for the benefit of a person who is a farmer`

@export Is my employer's business an agricultural enterprise under regulation 9(1)?
GIVEN `it is the business of agriculture` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the business of agriculture (see the question on regulation 9(1) "agriculture")?
      `it is carried on for the benefit of a person who is a farmer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it carried on for the benefit of a person who is a farmer?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my employer's business an agricultural enterprise under regulation 9(1)` IF
    `reg 9(1) agricultural enterprise` `it is the business of agriculture` `it is carried on for the benefit of a person who is a farmer`

@export Is my work horticulture under regulation 9(1)?
GIVEN operation IS A `er1 Operation that the definition of horticulture describes` @desc Which of these is your work? Choose the one that fits, or the last choice if none of them does.
      `the landscape gardening is incidental to the horticulture operations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your work is landscape gardening: is it incidental to the propagating, producing, raising or harvesting of vegetables, flowers, shrubs, ornamental grasses or their seeds, seedlings, grafts or cuttings?
      `the landscape gardening is incidental to agriculture` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your work is landscape gardening: is it incidental to the carrying out of agriculture?
      `the services are performed at the place where the operations are carried on` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your work is a service that goes with those operations: is it performed at the place where the operations are carried on?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my work horticulture under regulation 9(1)` IF
    `reg 9(1) horticulture` operation `the landscape gardening is incidental to the horticulture operations` `the landscape gardening is incidental to agriculture` `the services are performed at the place where the operations are carried on`

@export Is my farm work excluded from insurable employment under regulation 9(2)?
GIVEN `my work would otherwise be insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would your work otherwise be insurable employment?
      `I am employed by the employer in agriculture` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed by the employer in agriculture?
      `I am employed by the employer in an agricultural enterprise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed by the employer in an agricultural enterprise?
      `I am employed by the employer in horticulture` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed by the employer in horticulture?
      `the number of days in a year that I am employed by the employer in that work` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days in a year are you employed by the employer in that work?
      `I am paid in cash by the employer for any part of that work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the employer pay you in cash for any part of that work?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my farm work excluded from insurable employment under regulation 9(2)` IF
    `reg 9(2) employment in agriculture, an agricultural enterprise or horticulture`
        `my work would otherwise be insurable employment`
        `I am employed by the employer in agriculture`
        `I am employed by the employer in an agricultural enterprise`
        `I am employed by the employer in horticulture`
        `the number of days in a year that I am employed by the employer in that work`
        `I am paid in cash by the employer for any part of that work`

§§ `Regulations 9.001 and 9.002 -- looking for suitable work`

-- Situation: you are claiming regular benefits and must show that you are making reasonable and customary efforts to find suitable
-- employment (the Commission's judgment on the evidence is not asked; these questions ask the facts the Regulations make decisive).

@export Are my efforts to find suitable work reasonable and customary efforts under regulation 9.001?
GIVEN `my efforts are sustained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your job-search efforts sustained?
      `my efforts include assessing employment opportunities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your efforts include assessing employment opportunities?
      `my efforts include preparing a resume or cover letter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your efforts include preparing a resume or cover letter?
      `my efforts include registering with job search tools, electronic job banks or employment agencies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your efforts include registering for job search tools or with electronic job banks or employment agencies?
      `my efforts include attending job search workshops or job fairs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your efforts include attending job search workshops or job fairs?
      `my efforts include networking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your efforts include networking?
      `my efforts include contacting prospective employers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your efforts include contacting prospective employers?
      `my efforts include submitting job applications` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your efforts include submitting job applications?
      `my efforts include attending interviews` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your efforts include attending interviews?
      `my efforts include undergoing evaluations of competencies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your efforts include undergoing evaluations of competencies?
      `my efforts are directed toward obtaining suitable employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your efforts directed toward obtaining suitable employment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are my efforts to find suitable work reasonable and customary efforts under regulation 9.001` IF
    `reg 9.001 the claimant's efforts to obtain suitable employment are reasonable and customary efforts`
        `my efforts are sustained`
        (`reg 9.001(b) the claimant's efforts consist of one or more of the listed kinds of effort`
            `my efforts include assessing employment opportunities`
            `my efforts include preparing a resume or cover letter`
            `my efforts include registering with job search tools, electronic job banks or employment agencies`
            `my efforts include attending job search workshops or job fairs`
            `my efforts include networking`
            `my efforts include contacting prospective employers`
            `my efforts include submitting job applications`
            `my efforts include attending interviews`
            `my efforts include undergoing evaluations of competencies`)
        `my efforts are directed toward obtaining suitable employment`

@export Is this job suitable employment for me under regulation 9.002?
GIVEN `my health and physical capabilities allow me to commute to the place of work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your health and physical capabilities allow you to commute to the place of work?
      `my health and physical capabilities allow me to perform the work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your health and physical capabilities allow you to perform the work?
      `the hours of work are incompatible with my family obligations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the hours of work incompatible with your family obligations?
      `the hours of work are incompatible with my religious beliefs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the hours of work incompatible with your religious beliefs?
      `the nature of the work is contrary to my moral convictions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the nature of the work contrary to your moral convictions?
      `the nature of the work is contrary to my religious beliefs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the nature of the work contrary to your religious beliefs?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this job suitable employment for me under regulation 9.002` IF
    `reg 9.002(1) suitable employment`
        `my health and physical capabilities allow me to commute to the place of work`
        `my health and physical capabilities allow me to perform the work`
        `the hours of work are incompatible with my family obligations`
        `the hours of work are incompatible with my religious beliefs`
        `the nature of the work is contrary to my moral convictions`
        `the nature of the work is contrary to my religious beliefs`

§§ `Regulations 9.01 and 9.02 -- ending my agreement with the Commission (self-employed persons)`

-- Situation: you are a self-employed person with an agreement with the Commission and are ending it, or taking back a notice to end it
-- (the form can ask "Are you a self-employed person who has an agreement with the Commission?" first).

@export Is my notice ending my agreement with the Commission in the form regulation 9.01 requires?
GIVEN `I give the Commission a notice to terminate the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you give the Commission a notice to terminate your agreement?
      `the notice is given in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice given in writing?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my notice ending my agreement with the Commission in the form regulation 9.01 requires` IF
    `reg 9.01 the notice to terminate the agreement is given in the form the Regulations require` `I give the Commission a notice to terminate the agreement` `the notice is given in writing`

@export Is my withdrawal of that notice in the form regulation 9.02 requires?
GIVEN `I give the Commission a withdrawal of the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you give the Commission a withdrawal of your notice to terminate the agreement?
      `the withdrawal is given in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the withdrawal given in writing?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my withdrawal of that notice in the form regulation 9.02 requires` IF
    `reg 9.02 the withdrawal of the notice is given in the form the Regulations require` `I give the Commission a withdrawal of the notice` `the withdrawal is given in writing`

§§ `Regulations 9.1 to 11 -- how many hours of insurable employment am I considered to have worked`

-- The hours the Act's tests count (ss 7 and 7.1) are worked out by these Regulations. One question asks which of regulations 9.1 and 10
-- applies and how many hours it gives for a period of employment; the questions after it cover unpaid earnings, standby and
-- presence at the premises, paid leave, and the deemed hours of regulation 11. The answer is hours, or no answer (NOTHING) where the
-- regulation does not fix them. Hours of paid leave and standby are added to hours worked by the person, not by these questions.

@export How many hours of insurable employment am I considered to have worked in this period of employment under regulations 9.1 and 10?
GIVEN `I am paid on an hourly basis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your earnings paid on an hourly basis?
      `the hours I worked at my ordinary rate of pay` IS A NUMBER @desc If you are paid by the hour: how many hours did you actually work, and get paid for, at your ordinary rate of pay?
      `the hours I worked at an overtime rate of pay` IS A NUMBER @desc If you are paid by the hour: how many of the hours you actually worked, and got paid for, were paid at an overtime rate? (each counts as one hour)
      `my employer provides evidence of the hours I worked and was paid for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are not paid by the hour: does your employer provide evidence of the number of hours you actually worked in the period and were paid for?
      `the number of hours my employer's evidence shows` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours does that evidence show?
      `my employer cannot establish with certainty the hours I worked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employer unable to establish with certainty the number of hours you worked, and were paid for, in the period?
      `my actual hours are not known or ascertainable by my employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your actual hours of work in the period not known to your employer and not something it can find out?
      `my employer and I agree on the number of hours that would normally be required to gain my earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you and your employer agreed on the number of hours that would normally be required to gain your earnings?
      `the agreed number of hours is reasonable in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the agreed number of hours reasonable in the circumstances?
      `the agreed number of hours` IS A NUMBER @desc What number of hours did you and your employer agree? (0 if none)
      `no agreement can be reached` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can no agreement be reached?
      `the Minister of National Revenue has established a number of hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister of National Revenue established the number of hours, by examining the terms of your employment and comparing it with workers doing similar work?
      `the number of hours the Minister of National Revenue has established` IS A NUMBER @desc What number of hours has the Minister of National Revenue established? (0 if none)
      `my total earnings for the period of employment` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your total earnings for the period of employment, in dollars?
      `the minimum wage that applied on January 1 of the year the earnings were payable` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the minimum wage, in dollars per hour, that applied on January 1 of the year in which the earnings were payable, in the province where you worked?
      `there is evidence that I worked overtime or excess hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there evidence that you worked overtime or excess hours?
      `the first day of my period of employment` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of your period of employment?
      `the last day of my period of employment` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of your period of employment?
      `regulation 10.1 fixes my hours for this period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the hours in question hours that regulation 10.1 fixes (paid leave, a lump sum for leave, or a paid non-working day)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many hours of insurable employment am I considered to have worked in this period of employment under regulations 9.1 and 10` IS
    `reg 9.1 and reg 10(1) to (6) the hours fixed by the first method that applies`
        `regulation 10.1 fixes my hours for this period`
        `the answer under reg 9.1`
        `the answer under reg 10(1)`
        `the answer under reg 10(4)`
        `the answer under reg 10(2)`
        `the answer under reg 10(3)`
    WHERE
        `the answer under reg 9.1` MEANS
            `reg 9.1 the hours considered to have been worked by a person paid on an hourly basis`
                `I am paid on an hourly basis`
                (`reg 10.2(a) the number of hours of insurable employment` `the hours I worked at my ordinary rate of pay` `the hours I worked at an overtime rate of pay`)
        `the answer under reg 10(1)` MEANS
            `reg 10(1) the hours deemed to have been worked where the employer provides evidence`
                (NOT (`I am paid on an hourly basis`))
                `my employer provides evidence of the hours I worked and was paid for`
                `the number of hours my employer's evidence shows`
        `section 9.1 applies` MEANS isJust `the answer under reg 9.1`
        `subsection (1) applies` MEANS isJust `the answer under reg 10(1)`
        `the situation of subsection (2) arises` MEANS
            `reg 10(2) the employer cannot establish the hours and neither subsection (1) nor section 9.1 applies`
                `subsection (1) applies` `section 9.1 applies` `my employer cannot establish with certainty the hours I worked`
        `the answer under reg 10(2)` MEANS
            `reg 10(2) the hours deemed to have been worked where the parties agree`
                `the situation of subsection (2) arises`
                `my employer and I agree on the number of hours that would normally be required to gain my earnings`
                `the agreed number of hours is reasonable in the circumstances`
                `the agreed number of hours`
        `the answer under reg 10(3)` MEANS
            IF `the Minister of National Revenue has established a number of hours`
            THEN `reg 10(3) the hours deemed to have been worked as established by the Minister of National Revenue`
                    `the situation of subsection (2) arises`
                    `my employer and I agree on the number of hours that would normally be required to gain my earnings`
                    `the agreed number of hours is reasonable in the circumstances`
                    `no agreement can be reached`
                    `the number of hours the Minister of National Revenue has established`
            ELSE NOTHING
        `the answer under reg 10(4)` MEANS
            `reg 10(4) the hours deemed to have been worked where the actual hours are not known`
                `subsection (1) applies` `section 9.1 applies`
                `my actual hours are not known or ascertainable by my employer`
                `my total earnings for the period of employment`
                `the minimum wage that applied on January 1 of the year the earnings were payable`
                `there is evidence that I worked overtime or excess hours`
                `the first day of my period of employment`
                `the last day of my period of employment`

@export How many hours am I considered to have worked where part of my pay for a period of work was never paid, under regulation 9.2?
GIVEN `my earnings or a part of them for the period remain unpaid for the reasons in subsection 2(2) of the Insurable Earnings and Collection of Premiums Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your earnings, or a part of them, for a period of insurable employment remain unpaid for the reasons described in subsection 2(2) of the Insurable Earnings and Collection of Premiums Regulations?
      `regulation 10 fixes my hours for the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the number of hours for the period fixed by regulation 10 (your employer shows the hours, you and your employer agree them, the Minister sets them, or they are worked out from your earnings)?
      `the number of hours I actually worked in the period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours did you actually work in the period, paid or not?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many hours am I considered to have worked where part of my pay for a period of work was never paid, under regulation 9.2` IS
    `reg 9.2 the hours deemed to have been worked where earnings remain unpaid`
        `my earnings or a part of them for the period remain unpaid for the reasons in subsection 2(2) of the Insurable Earnings and Collection of Premiums Regulations`
        `regulation 10 fixes my hours for the period`
        `the number of hours I actually worked in the period`

@export How many hours of standby or presence at the premises count as hours of insurable employment under regulation 10.01?
GIVEN `my contract requires me to be available awaiting a request from my employer to work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your contract of employment require you to be available for a certain period awaiting a request from your employer to work?
      `the rate at which I am paid for those hours` IS A NUMBER @desc At what rate per hour, in dollars, are you paid for the hours you are required to be available? (0 if not paid)
      `the rate I would be paid if I had actually worked` IS A NUMBER @desc What rate per hour, in dollars, would you be paid if you had actually worked during that period?
      `the number of hours I am required to be available` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours is the period in which you are required to be available?
      `my employer requires me to be present at its premises in case my services are required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your employer require you under your contract to be present at its premises for a certain period in case your services are required?
      `I am paid for the hours I am required to be present` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you paid for those hours?
      `the number of hours I am required to be present` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours is the period in which you are required to be present?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many hours of standby or presence at the premises count as hours of insurable employment under regulation 10.01` IS
    `reg 10.01 the hours deemed to be hours of insurable employment`
        (`reg 10.01(2) the hours of presence at the premises deemed to be hours of insurable employment`
            `my employer requires me to be present at its premises in case my services are required`
            `I am paid for the hours I am required to be present`
            `the number of hours I am required to be present`)
        (`reg 10.01(1) the hours of availability deemed to be hours of insurable employment`
            `my contract requires me to be available awaiting a request from my employer to work`
            `the rate at which I am paid for those hours`
            `the rate I would be paid if I had actually worked`
            `the number of hours I am required to be available`)

@export How many hours am I considered to have worked during a period of paid leave under regulation 10.1(1)?
GIVEN `my employer pays me for a period of paid leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your employer pay you for a period of paid leave?
      `the hours I would normally have worked and been paid for during that period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours would you normally have worked, and been paid for, during that period?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many hours am I considered to have worked during a period of paid leave under regulation 10.1(1)` IS
    `reg 10.1(1) the hours deemed to have been worked during a period of paid leave` `my employer pays me for a period of paid leave` `the hours I would normally have worked and been paid for during that period`

@export How many hours am I considered to have worked during leave paid as a lump sum under regulation 10.1(2)?
GIVEN `my employer pays me for a period of leave as a lump sum calculated without regard to the length of the leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your employer pay you for a period of leave as a lump sum calculated without regard to the length of the leave?
      `the hours I would normally have worked and been paid for during that period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours would you normally have worked, and been paid for, during that period?
      `the lump sum` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the lump sum, in dollars?
      `the part of the lump sum that is excluded from my earnings by subsection 2(3) of the Insurable Earnings and Collection of Premiums Regulations` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of the lump sum, in dollars, is excluded from your earnings from insurable employment by subsection 2(3) of the Insurable Earnings and Collection of Premiums Regulations? (0 if none)
      `my normal hourly rate of pay` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your normal hourly rate of pay, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many hours am I considered to have worked during leave paid as a lump sum under regulation 10.1(2)` IS
    `reg 10.1(2) the hours deemed to have been worked during a period of leave paid as a lump sum`
        `my employer pays me for a period of leave as a lump sum calculated without regard to the length of the leave`
        `the hours I would normally have worked and been paid for during that period`
        `the lump sum`
        `the part of the lump sum that is excluded from my earnings by subsection 2(3) of the Insurable Earnings and Collection of Premiums Regulations`
        `my normal hourly rate of pay`

@export How many hours am I considered to have worked on a non-working day my employer pays me for under regulation 10.1(3)?
GIVEN `my employer pays me for a non-working day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your employer pay you for a non-working day?
      `I work on that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you work on that day?
      `the hours I actually worked on that day` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours did you actually work on that day? (0 if none)
      `the hours I would normally have worked on that day` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours would you normally have worked on that day?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many hours am I considered to have worked on a non-working day my employer pays me for under regulation 10.1(3)` IS
    `reg 10.1(3) the hours deemed to have been worked on a non-working day`
        `my employer pays me for a non-working day` `I work on that day` `the hours I actually worked on that day` `the hours I would normally have worked on that day`

@export How many hours a week am I considered to work if my occupation limits full-time hours under regulation 11(1)?
GIVEN `I am employed on a full-time basis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed on a full-time basis?
      `the hours per week I am paid for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours per week are you paid for?
      `a statute limits the full-time hours of my occupation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the maximum number of hours of full-time work per week in your occupation limited by federal or provincial statutes, or regulations made under those statutes?
      `that statutory maximum number of hours per week` IS A NUMBER @desc What is that maximum number of hours per week? (0 if there is none)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many hours a week am I considered to work if my occupation limits full-time hours under regulation 11(1)` IS
    `reg 11(1) the hours per week deemed to be worked in an occupation with limited full-time hours`
        `I am employed on a full-time basis` `the hours per week I am paid for` `a statute limits the full-time hours of my occupation` `that statutory maximum number of hours per week`

@export How many hours a week am I considered to work if I am a member of the Canadian Forces or a police force on standby under regulation 11(2)(a)?
GIVEN `regulation 10 fixes my hours for the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the number of hours for the week fixed by regulation 10 (your employer shows the hours, you and your employer agree them, the Minister sets them, or they are worked out from your earnings)?
      `I am a member of the Canadian Forces on full-time service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the Canadian Forces on full-time service?
      `I am a member of a police force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of a police force?
      `I am required to be available on standby outside of my regularly scheduled hours of work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you required to be available on standby outside of your regularly scheduled hours of work?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many hours a week am I considered to work if I am a member of the Canadian Forces or a police force on standby under regulation 11(2)(a)` IS
    `reg 11(2)(a) the hours per week deemed to be worked by a member of the Canadian Forces or of a police force on standby`
        `regulation 10 fixes my hours for the week` `I am a member of the Canadian Forces on full-time service` `I am a member of a police force` `I am required to be available on standby outside of my regularly scheduled hours of work`

@export How many hours a week am I considered to work if I am a member of the reserve force under regulation 11(2)(b)?
GIVEN `regulation 10 fixes my hours for the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the number of hours for the week fixed by regulation 10 (your employer shows the hours, you and your employer agree them, the Minister sets them, or they are worked out from your earnings)?
      `I am a member of the reserve force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the reserve force?
      `I am paid the rate of pay for each period of duty or training` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you paid the rate of pay for each period of duty or training?
      `the number of my periods of duty or training of less than 6 hours in the week` IS A NUMBER @desc In the week, how many periods of duty or training of less than 6 hours did you have?
      `the number of my periods of duty or training of 6 to 24 hours in the week` IS A NUMBER @desc In the week, how many periods of duty or training of not less than 6 hours and not more than 24 hours did you have?
      `the number of my periods of duty or training of more than 24 hours in the week` IS A NUMBER @desc In the week, how many periods of duty or training of more than 24 hours did you have?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many hours a week am I considered to work if I am a member of the reserve force under regulation 11(2)(b)` IS
    `reg 11(2)(b) the hours per week deemed to be worked by a member of the reserve force`
        `regulation 10 fixes my hours for the week` `I am a member of the reserve force` `I am paid the rate of pay for each period of duty or training`
        `the number of my periods of duty or training of less than 6 hours in the week`
        `the number of my periods of duty or training of 6 to 24 hours in the week`
        `the number of my periods of duty or training of more than 24 hours in the week`

§§ `Regulations 11.1 and 13 -- the self-employed earnings threshold and the average number of weeks`

-- Situation: you are self-employed (Part VII.1 of the Act), or you have had an overpayment because of a violation (the form can ask
-- "Are you self-employed, or have you been found to have committed a violation?" first). The figures are the Commission's published ones.

@export What is the adjusted amount of self-employed earnings for the year under regulation 11.1?
GIVEN `the amount before this year's adjustment` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the amount last year after its adjustment, in dollars? (For the first adjustment, on January 1, 2012, use the amount of self-employed earnings in subparagraph 152.07(1)(d)(i) of the Act.)
      `this year's ratio referred to in paragraph 4(2)(b) of the Act` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the ratio for this year referred to in paragraph 4(2)(b) of the Act (the Commission publishes it; for example 1.02)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the adjusted amount of self-employed earnings for the year under regulation 11.1` IS
    `reg 11.1(1) the adjusted amount for the year` `the amount before this year's adjustment` `this year's ratio referred to in paragraph 4(2)(b) of the Act`

@export What is my average number of weeks of regular benefits under regulation 13(1)?
GIVEN `the maximum number of weeks of benefits that may be paid to me` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid to you under section 8 of the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations or subsection 12(2) of the Act?
      `the number of weeks of benefits paid to me` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of benefits have been paid to you, including the weeks used to establish the overpayment under paragraph 7.1(6)(a) of the Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my average number of weeks of regular benefits under regulation 13(1)` IS
    `reg 13(1) the average number of weeks of regular benefits of a claimant` `the maximum number of weeks of benefits that may be paid to me` `the number of weeks of benefits paid to me`

@export What is my average number of weeks of benefits as a self-employed person under regulation 13(2)?
GIVEN `the maximum number of weeks of benefits that may be paid to me under subsection 152.14(1)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid to you under subsection 152.14(1) of the Act?
      `the number of weeks of benefits paid to me` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of benefits have been paid to you, including the weeks used to establish the overpayment referred to in paragraph 152.07(3)(a) of the Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my average number of weeks of benefits as a self-employed person under regulation 13(2)` IS
    `reg 13(2) the average number of weeks of benefits of a self-employed person` `the maximum number of weeks of benefits that may be paid to me under subsection 152.14(1)` `the number of weeks of benefits paid to me`

§§ `Regulation 14 -- has an interruption of my earnings occurred, and on what day`

-- An interruption of earnings is what starts a benefit period (s 10 of the Act, piece ei1). The first question asks whether one has
-- occurred; the questions after it give the day where the Regulations state one.

@export Has an interruption of my earnings occurred under regulation 14?
GIVEN `I am an insured person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an insured person (are you, or have you been, in insurable employment)?
      `this follows a period of employment with an employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does this follow a period of employment with an employer?
      `I was laid off` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you laid off?
      `I was separated from that employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you separated from that employment?
      `the number of consecutive days with no work for that employer and no earnings from that job` IS A NUMBER @desc How many consecutive days have you had during which no work is performed for that employer and no earnings that arise from that employment (other than earnings described in subsection 36(13)) are payable or allocated?
      `my normal weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your normal weekly earnings from that employment, in dollars?
      `my earnings for the week` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your earnings from that employment for the week in which they fell, in dollars?
      `I ceased to work in that employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you cease to work in that employment?
      `the reason I ceased to work` IS A `er1 Reason an insured person ceases to work` @desc Why did you cease to work? Choose illness, injury or quarantine; pregnancy; the need to care for a child; the need to care for a family member; the need to care for a critically ill child; the need to care for a critically ill adult; or another reason.
      `a day in the week in which my earnings fell` IS A DATE @desc What is any day of the week in which your earnings fell?
      `I am employed under a contract of employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed under a contract of employment?
      `my usual remuneration is payable under my contract of employment for a period of this many days` IS A NUMBER @desc If you are employed under a contract of employment: for a period of how many days is your usual remuneration payable? (0 if you have no such contract)
      `the time in question falls during that period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the time in question fall during that period?
      `the period is a period of leave referred to in subsection 11(4) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the period a period of leave referred to in subsection 11(4) of the Act?
      `the period is a period of leave referred to in subsection 11(3) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the period a period of leave referred to in subsection 11(3) of the Act?
      `I am employed in the sale or purchase of real estate on a commission basis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed in the sale or purchase of real estate on a commission basis?
      `I hold a licence to sell real estate issued by a provincial authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold a licence to sell real estate issued by a provincial authority?
      `my licence is surrendered, suspended or revoked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your licence surrendered, suspended or revoked?
      `my earnings from that employment consist mainly of commissions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your earnings from that employment consist mainly of commissions?
      `my contract of employment is terminated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract of employment terminated?
      `the day my licence was lost, my contract ended or I stopped working` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your licence surrendered, suspended or revoked, your contract terminated, or did you cease to work?
      `I accepted less remunerative work with my employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you accept less remunerative work with your employer?
      `I receive a wage supplement under a provincial law because the continuation of my work is a physical danger` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As a consequence, do you receive a wage supplement under a provincial law intended to provide indemnity payments where the continuation of your work represents a physical danger to you, your unborn child or the child you are breast-feeding?
      `my last day of work before the less remunerative work began` IS A DATE @desc What was your last day of work before the less remunerative work began?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has an interruption of my earnings occurred under regulation 14` IF
    `reg 14 an interruption of earnings has occurred`
        (`reg 14(1) an interruption of earnings occurs on lay-off or separation`
            `I am an insured person` `this follows a period of employment with an employer` `I was laid off` `I was separated from that employment`
            `the number of consecutive days with no work for that employer and no earnings from that job`)
        (`reg 14(2) the day on which an interruption of earnings occurs because of a reduction in earnings`
            `I am an insured person` `a day in the week in which my earnings fell` `my normal weekly earnings` `my earnings for the week`
            `I ceased to work in that employment` `the reason I ceased to work`)
        (`reg 14(5)(a) the day on which an interruption of earnings occurs for a real estate salesperson on commission`
            `I am employed in the sale or purchase of real estate on a commission basis` `I hold a licence to sell real estate issued by a provincial authority`
            `my licence is surrendered, suspended or revoked`
            (`I ceased to work in that employment` AND `reg 14(2) the reason is a circumstance listed in subsection (2)` `the reason I ceased to work`)
            `the day my licence was lost, my contract ended or I stopped working`)
        (`reg 14(5)(b) the day on which an interruption of earnings occurs for a person whose earnings are mainly commissions`
            `I am employed under a contract of employment`
            `my earnings from that employment consist mainly of commissions` `my contract of employment is terminated`
            (`I ceased to work in that employment` AND `reg 14(2) the reason is a circumstance listed in subsection (2)` `the reason I ceased to work`)
            `the day my licence was lost, my contract ended or I stopped working`)
        (`reg 14(7) the day on which an interruption of earnings occurs when less remunerative work is accepted`
            `I accepted less remunerative work with my employer`
            `I receive a wage supplement under a provincial law because the continuation of my work is a physical danger`
            `my last day of work before the less remunerative work began`)
        (`reg 14(3) a period of leave referred to in subsection 11(4) of the Act does not constitute an interruption of earnings` `the period is a period of leave referred to in subsection 11(4) of the Act`)
        (`reg 14(4) no interruption of earnings occurs during a period greater than a week for which the usual remuneration is payable`
            `I am employed under a contract of employment`
            `my usual remuneration is payable under my contract of employment for a period of this many days`
            `the time in question falls during that period`)
        (`reg 14(6) a period of leave referred to in subsection 11(3) of the Act does not constitute an interruption of earnings` `the period is a period of leave referred to in subsection 11(3) of the Act`)

@export On what day does an interruption of my earnings occur because my earnings fell, under regulation 14(2)?
GIVEN `I am an insured person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an insured person (are you, or have you been, in insurable employment)?
      `a day in the week in which my earnings fell` IS A DATE @desc What is any day of the week in which your earnings fell?
      `my normal weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your normal weekly earnings from that employment, in dollars?
      `my earnings for the week` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your earnings from that employment for that week, in dollars?
      `I ceased to work in that employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you cease to work in that employment?
      `the reason I ceased to work` IS A `er1 Reason an insured person ceases to work` @desc Why did you cease to work? Choose illness, injury or quarantine; pregnancy; the need to care for a child; the need to care for a family member; the need to care for a critically ill child; the need to care for a critically ill adult; or another reason.
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what day does an interruption of my earnings occur because my earnings fell, under regulation 14(2)` IS
    `reg 14(2) the day on which an interruption of earnings occurs because of a reduction in earnings`
        `I am an insured person` `a day in the week in which my earnings fell` `my normal weekly earnings` `my earnings for the week` `I ceased to work in that employment` `the reason I ceased to work`

@export On what day does an interruption of my earnings occur if I sell real estate on commission, under regulation 14(5)(a)?
GIVEN `I am employed in the sale or purchase of real estate on a commission basis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed in the sale or purchase of real estate on a commission basis?
      `I hold a licence to sell real estate issued by a provincial authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold a licence to sell real estate issued by a provincial authority?
      `my licence is surrendered, suspended or revoked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your licence surrendered, suspended or revoked?
      `I ceased to work in that employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you cease to work in that employment?
      `the reason I ceased to work` IS A `er1 Reason an insured person ceases to work` @desc Why did you cease to work? Choose illness, injury or quarantine; pregnancy; the need to care for a child; the need to care for a family member; the need to care for a critically ill child; the need to care for a critically ill adult; or another reason.
      `the day that happens` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your licence surrendered, suspended or revoked, or did you cease to work?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what day does an interruption of my earnings occur if I sell real estate on commission, under regulation 14(5)(a)` IS
    `reg 14(5)(a) the day on which an interruption of earnings occurs for a real estate salesperson on commission`
        `I am employed in the sale or purchase of real estate on a commission basis` `I hold a licence to sell real estate issued by a provincial authority` `my licence is surrendered, suspended or revoked`
        (`I ceased to work in that employment` AND `reg 14(2) the reason is a circumstance listed in subsection (2)` `the reason I ceased to work`)
        `the day that happens`

@export On what day does an interruption of my earnings occur if my earnings are mainly commissions, under regulation 14(5)(b)?
GIVEN `I am employed under a contract of employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed under a contract of employment?
      `my earnings from that employment consist mainly of commissions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your earnings from that employment consist mainly of commissions?
      `my contract of employment is terminated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract of employment terminated?
      `I ceased to work in that employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you cease to work in that employment?
      `the reason I ceased to work` IS A `er1 Reason an insured person ceases to work` @desc Why did you cease to work? Choose illness, injury or quarantine; pregnancy; the need to care for a child; the need to care for a family member; the need to care for a critically ill child; the need to care for a critically ill adult; or another reason.
      `the day that happens` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your contract terminated, or did you cease to work?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what day does an interruption of my earnings occur if my earnings are mainly commissions, under regulation 14(5)(b)` IS
    `reg 14(5)(b) the day on which an interruption of earnings occurs for a person whose earnings are mainly commissions`
        `I am employed under a contract of employment` `my earnings from that employment consist mainly of commissions` `my contract of employment is terminated`
        (`I ceased to work in that employment` AND `reg 14(2) the reason is a circumstance listed in subsection (2)` `the reason I ceased to work`)
        `the day that happens`

@export On what day does an interruption of my earnings occur if I accept less remunerative work, under regulation 14(7)?
GIVEN `I accepted less remunerative work with my employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you accept less remunerative work with your employer?
      `I receive a wage supplement under a provincial law because the continuation of my work is a physical danger` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As a consequence, do you receive a wage supplement under a provincial law intended to provide indemnity payments where the continuation of your work represents a physical danger to you, your unborn child or the child you are breast-feeding?
      `my last day of work before the less remunerative work began` IS A DATE @desc What was your last day of work before the less remunerative work began?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what day does an interruption of my earnings occur if I accept less remunerative work, under regulation 14(7)` IS
    `reg 14(7) the day on which an interruption of earnings occurs when less remunerative work is accepted`
        `I accepted less remunerative work with my employer`
        `I receive a wage supplement under a provincial law because the continuation of my work is a physical danger`
        `my last day of work before the less remunerative work began`

@export On what day does an interruption of my earnings as a self-employed person occur under regulation 14.01?
GIVEN `I am a self-employed person referred to in paragraph 152.07(1)(c) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a self-employed person referred to in paragraph 152.07(1)(c) of the Act?
      `a day in the week in which I declare the reduction` IS A DATE @desc What is any day of the week in which you declare having reduced the time you devote to your business activities?
      `the normal level of time I devote to my business activities, in hours per week` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the normal level of time you devote to your business activities, in hours per week?
      `the time I devoted to my business activities in the week of the reduction, in hours` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours did you devote to your business activities in that week?
      `I declare having reduced the time I devote to my business activities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you declare having reduced the time you devote to your business activities?
      `I cease to work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you cease to work?
      `the reason I cease to work` IS A `er1 Reason a self-employed person ceases to work` @desc Why do you cease to work? Choose illness, injury or quarantine; pregnancy; the need to care for a child; the need to care for a family member; the need to care for a critically ill child; the need to care for a critically ill adult; or another reason.
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what day does an interruption of my earnings as a self-employed person occur under regulation 14.01` IS
    `reg 14.01 the day on which an interruption of earnings of a self-employed person occurs`
        `I am a self-employed person referred to in paragraph 152.07(1)(c) of the Act`
        `a day in the week in which I declare the reduction`
        `the normal level of time I devote to my business activities, in hours per week`
        `the time I devoted to my business activities in the week of the reduction, in hours`
        `I declare having reduced the time I devote to my business activities`
        `I cease to work`
        `the reason I cease to work`

§§ `Regulations 14.1 and 16 -- undeclared earnings, and allowances while on a course`

-- Situation (14.1): you failed to declare earnings that were allocated to a period that began before August 12, 2001. Situation
-- (16): you attend a course or program of instruction or training, or were paid under Part II of the Act for weeks that you later
-- receive regular benefits for (the form can ask "Have you attended a course or program, or received an allowance for one?" first).

@export On what day does the period to which my undeclared earnings are allocated end under regulation 14.1?
GIVEN `I failed to declare earnings that are allocated to a period referred to in paragraph 15(4)(a), (b) or (c) as it read before August 12, 2001` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are earnings you failed to declare being allocated to a period referred to in paragraph 15(4)(a), (b) or (c), as that paragraph read immediately before August 12, 2001?
      `the first day of that period` IS A DATE @desc On what day did that period begin?
      `the day on which that period was to have ended under that paragraph` IS A DATE @desc On what day was that period to have ended under that paragraph?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what day does the period to which my undeclared earnings are allocated end under regulation 14.1` IS
    `reg 14.1 the day on which the period ends` `I failed to declare earnings that are allocated to a period referred to in paragraph 15(4)(a), (b) or (c) as it read before August 12, 2001` `the first day of that period` `the day on which that period was to have ended under that paragraph`

@export How much will be deducted from my benefits for a week I attend a course or program under regulation 16(1) and (2)?
GIVEN `the week is a week of unemployment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the week a week of unemployment?
      `I am attending the course or program during the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you attending a course or program of instruction or training during the week?
      `allowances are payable to me for the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are allowances payable to you for the week for attending it?
      `the Commission or an authority it designated has referred me to the course or program` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission, or an authority designated by the Commission, referred you to the course or program?
      `the total allowances payable to me for attending it` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total amount of the allowances payable to you for attending the course or program, in dollars?
      `the amounts paid to me for dependant care, travel, commuting, living away from home or disability` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that was paid to you for dependant care, travel, commuting, living away from home or disability, in dollars? (0 if none)
      `I am entitled to work-sharing benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to work-sharing benefits?
      `the amounts paid to me using financial assistance under section 61 of the Act` IS A NUMBER @desc If you are entitled to work-sharing benefits: how much of that was paid to you using financial assistance provided under section 61 of the Act to implement employment support measures for claimants entitled to work-sharing benefits, in dollars? (0 if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much will be deducted from my benefits for a week I attend a course or program under regulation 16(1) and (2)` IS
    `reg 16(1) the amount deducted from the benefits for a week of unemployment while attending a course or program`
        `the week is a week of unemployment`
        `I am attending the course or program during the week`
        `allowances are payable to me for the week`
        `the Commission or an authority it designated has referred me to the course or program`
        (`reg 16(2) the allowances referred to in subsection (1)`
            `the total allowances payable to me for attending it`
            `the amounts paid to me for dependant care, travel, commuting, living away from home or disability`
            `I am entitled to work-sharing benefits`
            `the amounts paid to me using financial assistance under section 61 of the Act`)

@export How much of what I was paid under Part II of the Act will be deducted from my benefits for the same weeks under regulation 16(3)?
GIVEN `I do not meet the qualifying conditions of section 7 or 7.1 of the Act or of the regulations made under Part VIII` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For those weeks, did you not meet the qualifying conditions of section 7 or 7.1 of the Act or of any regulations made under Part VIII of the Act?
      `I am disentitled within the meaning of subsection 6(1) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For those weeks, were you disentitled within the meaning of subsection 6(1) of the Act?
      `I am disqualified within the meaning of subsection 6(1) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For those weeks, were you disqualified within the meaning of subsection 6(1) of the Act?
      `I was paid earnings or allowances under Part II of the Act for weeks of a course or program` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you paid earnings or allowances under Part II of the Act for certain weeks for attending a course or program of instruction or training?
      `I was paid earnings from an employment support measure that gave me work experience` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you paid earnings from employment for certain weeks under an employment support measure referred to in paragraph 59(b) of the Act that is established to provide insured participants with employment opportunities through which they can gain work experience to improve their long-term employment prospects?
      `I later became entitled to regular benefits for the same weeks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you later become entitled to regular benefits for the same weeks as those for which you were paid those amounts?
      `the total I was paid under Part II of the Act for those weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total amount of earnings and allowances you were paid under Part II of the Act for those weeks, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of what I was paid under Part II of the Act will be deducted from my benefits for the same weeks under regulation 16(3)` IS
    `reg 16(3) the amount deducted from the benefits for the weeks for which Part II earnings or allowances were paid`
        `I do not meet the qualifying conditions of section 7 or 7.1 of the Act or of the regulations made under Part VIII`
        `I am disentitled within the meaning of subsection 6(1) of the Act`
        `I am disqualified within the meaning of subsection 6(1) of the Act`
        `I was paid earnings or allowances under Part II of the Act for weeks of a course or program`
        `I was paid earnings from an employment support measure that gave me work experience`
        `I later became entitled to regular benefits for the same weeks`
        `the total I was paid under Part II of the Act for those weeks`

§§ `Regulations 17 and 17.1 -- the regional rate of unemployment that applies to me`

-- The rate fixes how many hours I need and how many weeks I can be paid (ss 7, 7.1, 12 and 14 and Part VIII of the Act). Rates are
-- fractions: 6.5% is 0.065. The first question works out the rate of my region from Statistics Canada's figures; the second says
-- which region's rate is mine; the third applies the special rules for two regions for claims from 2000 to 2012.

@export What is the regional rate of unemployment for my region from Statistics Canada's figures under regulation 17(1)?
GIVEN `the number of the section of Schedule I that describes my region` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of the section of Schedule I of the Regulations (2 to 14) that describes your region?
      `Statistics Canada publishes the rate for my region` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Statistics Canada publish the rate of unemployment for your region (it may not, for reasons of confidentiality)?
      `the rates include the estimate for status Indians living on Indian reserves` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the monthly rates you give Statistics Canada's regional rates that include an estimate of the rates of unemployment for status Indians living on Indian reserves?
      `the rate for the third last month` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the seasonally adjusted rate of unemployment for your region for the third last month for which Statistics Canada produced statistics before the week your benefit period begins? (a fraction: 6.5% is 0.065)
      `the rate for the second last month` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the rate for the second last such month?
      `the rate for the last month` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the rate for the last such month?
      `the average of the rates for the last 12 months` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the average of the seasonally adjusted monthly rates for the last 12-month period for which Statistics Canada produced statistics before that week? (only needed for regions in sections 12 to 14 of Schedule I)
      `Statistics Canada has determined an average for my region` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If Statistics Canada does not publish the rate for your region, has it determined an average based on the minimum number of unemployed persons required to allow it to publish the rate?
      `the average Statistics Canada determined for the last three months` IS A NUMBER @desc What is that average for the last three-month period? (0 if none)
      `the average Statistics Canada determined for the last 12 months` IS A NUMBER @desc What is that average for the last 12-month period? (0 if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the regional rate of unemployment for my region from Statistics Canada's figures under regulation 17(1)` IS
    `reg 17(1) the regional rate of unemployment that applies to a claimant, for a region`
        `the number of the section of Schedule I that describes my region`
        (`reg 17(1) the average of the seasonally adjusted monthly rates of unemployment for the period`
            3 `the rates include the estimate for status Indians living on Indian reserves` `Statistics Canada publishes the rate for my region`
            (LIST `the rate for the third last month`, `the rate for the second last month`, `the rate for the last month`)
            `the three-month average Statistics Canada determined`)
        (`reg 17(1) the average of the monthly rates for the period, once worked out`
            `the rates include the estimate for status Indians living on Indian reserves` `Statistics Canada publishes the rate for my region`
            `the average of the rates for the last 12 months`
            `the 12-month average Statistics Canada determined`)
    WHERE
        `the three-month average Statistics Canada determined` MEANS
            IF `Statistics Canada has determined an average for my region` THEN JUST `the average Statistics Canada determined for the last three months` ELSE NOTHING
        `the 12-month average Statistics Canada determined` MEANS
            IF `Statistics Canada has determined an average for my region` THEN JUST `the average Statistics Canada determined for the last 12 months` ELSE NOTHING

@export Which regional rate of unemployment applies to me, given the region I lived or last worked in, under regulation 17(1.1) to (3)?
GIVEN purpose IS A `er1 Provision for which the regional rate of unemployment is needed` @desc For which provision of the Act is the rate needed? Choose section 7 (hours required), section 7.1, section 12 (weeks of benefits), section 14, Part VIII (fishing), or another provision.
      `I was ordinarily resident outside Canada during the week my benefit period begins` IS A BOOLEAN @desc During the week referred to in subsection 10(1) of the Act (the week your benefit period begins), were you ordinarily resident outside Canada?
      `it cannot be determined with certainty which region applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you ordinarily reside (or, if you live outside Canada, were you last employed in insurable employment in Canada) so near the boundaries of more than one region that it cannot be determined with certainty in which region?
      `the rate of my region` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the regional rate of unemployment of your region under regulation 17(1) (a fraction: 6.5% is 0.065)?
      `I live or worked near the boundary of a second region` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you live, or did you last work, near the boundary of a second region?
      `the rate of the second region` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the regional rate of unemployment of the second region? (0 if none)
      `I live or worked near the boundary of a third region` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you live, or did you last work, near the boundary of a third region?
      `the rate of the third region` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the regional rate of unemployment of the third region? (0 if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Which regional rate of unemployment applies to me, given the region I lived or last worked in, under regulation 17(1.1) to (3)` IS
    `reg 17(1.1) the regional rate of unemployment that applies to a claimant`
        purpose
        `I was ordinarily resident outside Canada during the week my benefit period begins`
        `it cannot be determined with certainty which region applies to me`
        `the rates of the regions concerned`
    WHERE
        `the rates of the regions concerned` MEANS
            `the rate of my region` FOLLOWED BY
                (IF `I live or worked near the boundary of a second region`
                 THEN `the rate of the second region` FOLLOWED BY
                        (IF `I live or worked near the boundary of a third region` THEN LIST `the rate of the third region` ELSE EMPTY)
                 ELSE EMPTY)

@export Which regional rate of unemployment applies to me under regulation 17.1 if my benefit period began between September 17, 2000 and April 7, 2012?
GIVEN purpose IS A `er1 Provision for which the regional rate of unemployment is needed` @desc For which provision of the Act is the rate needed? Choose section 7 (hours required), section 7.1, section 12 (weeks of benefits), section 14, Part VIII (fishing), or another provision.
      `I was ordinarily resident outside Canada during the week my benefit period begins` IS A BOOLEAN @desc During the week referred to in subsection 10(1) of the Act (the week your benefit period begins), were you ordinarily resident outside Canada?
      `the Sunday that begins the week referred to in subsection 10(1) of the Act` IS A DATE @desc What is the Sunday that begins the week referred to in subsection 10(1) of the Act (the week your benefit period begins)?
      `my region` IS A `er1 Region named in regulation 17.1` @desc Which region were you ordinarily resident in during that week (or, if you were ordinarily resident outside Canada, last employed in insurable employment in Canada in)? Choose Gaspesie - Iles-de-la-Madeleine, Lower St. Lawrence and North Shore, Madawaska - Charlotte, Restigouche - Albert, or a region not named in regulation 17.1.
      `my region's regional rate of unemployment under regulation 17(1)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the regional rate of unemployment of your region under regulation 17(1) (a fraction: 6.5% is 0.065)?
      `the neighbouring region's regional rate of unemployment under regulation 17(1)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the regional rate of unemployment under regulation 17(1) of the neighbouring region (Restigouche - Albert for Madawaska - Charlotte; Gaspesie - Iles-de-la-Madeleine for Lower St. Lawrence and North Shore)?
      `there was a first day after March 12, 2011 on which the hours and weeks were exactly the same` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there a day after March 12, 2011 on which the required number of hours of insurable employment and the number of weeks for which benefits are payable, for your region, were exactly the same using the special rate as using the regional rate under regulation 17(1)?
      `the first such day` IS A DATE @desc What was the first such day? (any date if there was none)
      `regulation 17(1.1) to (3) gives me a rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 17(1.1) to (3) give you a regional rate of unemployment (the previous question)?
      `the rate regulation 17(1.1) to (3) gives me` IS A NUMBER @desc What is that rate? (0 if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Which regional rate of unemployment applies to me under regulation 17.1 if my benefit period began between September 17, 2000 and April 7, 2012` IS
    `reg 17 and reg 17.1 the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the claimant`
        (`reg 17.1 the first answer that applies` `the special rates that could apply`)
        `the rate that regulation 17(1.1) to (3) gives`
    WHERE
        `the day the special rates cease` MEANS
            `reg 17.1(16) and (17) the Sunday after the day on which the hours and weeks are exactly the same`
                (IF `there was a first day after March 12, 2011 on which the hours and weeks were exactly the same` THEN JUST `the first such day` ELSE NOTHING)
        `the rate that regulation 17(1.1) to (3) gives` MEANS
            IF `regulation 17(1.1) to (3) gives me a rate` THEN JUST `the rate regulation 17(1.1) to (3) gives me` ELSE NOTHING
        `the special rates that could apply` MEANS
            IF `I was ordinarily resident outside Canada during the week my benefit period begins`
            THEN LIST `the answer under reg 17.1(3)`, `the answer under reg 17.1(5)`, `the answer under reg 17.1(7)`, `the answer under reg 17.1(9)`, `the answer under reg 17.1(11)`, `the answer under reg 17.1(13)`
            ELSE LIST `the answer under reg 17.1(2)`, `the answer under reg 17.1(4)`, `the answer under reg 17.1(6)`, `the answer under reg 17.1(8)`, `the answer under reg 17.1(10)`, `the answer under reg 17.1(12)`
        `the answer under reg 17.1(2)` MEANS `reg 17.1(2) the applicable regional rate for a claimant resident in Madawaska - Charlotte from September 17, 2000 to October 6, 2001` purpose `the Sunday that begins the week referred to in subsection 10(1) of the Act` `my region` `my region's regional rate of unemployment under regulation 17(1)` `the neighbouring region's regional rate of unemployment under regulation 17(1)`
        `the answer under reg 17.1(3)` MEANS `reg 17.1(3) the applicable regional rate for a claimant outside Canada last employed in Madawaska - Charlotte from September 17, 2000 to October 6, 2001` purpose `the Sunday that begins the week referred to in subsection 10(1) of the Act` `my region` `my region's regional rate of unemployment under regulation 17(1)` `the neighbouring region's regional rate of unemployment under regulation 17(1)`
        `the answer under reg 17.1(4)` MEANS `reg 17.1(4) the applicable regional rate for a claimant resident in Madawaska - Charlotte from October 7, 2001 to October 12, 2002` purpose `the Sunday that begins the week referred to in subsection 10(1) of the Act` `my region` `my region's regional rate of unemployment under regulation 17(1)` `the neighbouring region's regional rate of unemployment under regulation 17(1)`
        `the answer under reg 17.1(5)` MEANS `reg 17.1(5) the applicable regional rate for a claimant outside Canada last employed in Madawaska - Charlotte from October 7, 2001 to October 12, 2002` purpose `the Sunday that begins the week referred to in subsection 10(1) of the Act` `my region` `my region's regional rate of unemployment under regulation 17(1)` `the neighbouring region's regional rate of unemployment under regulation 17(1)`
        `the answer under reg 17.1(6)` MEANS `reg 17.1(6) the applicable regional rate for a claimant resident in Madawaska - Charlotte from October 13, 2002 to April 7, 2012` purpose `the Sunday that begins the week referred to in subsection 10(1) of the Act` `my region` `my region's regional rate of unemployment under regulation 17(1)` `the neighbouring region's regional rate of unemployment under regulation 17(1)` `the day the special rates cease`
        `the answer under reg 17.1(7)` MEANS `reg 17.1(7) the applicable regional rate for a claimant outside Canada last employed in Madawaska - Charlotte from October 13, 2002 to April 7, 2012` purpose `the Sunday that begins the week referred to in subsection 10(1) of the Act` `my region` `my region's regional rate of unemployment under regulation 17(1)` `the neighbouring region's regional rate of unemployment under regulation 17(1)` `the day the special rates cease`
        `the answer under reg 17.1(8)` MEANS `reg 17.1(8) the applicable regional rate for a claimant resident in Lower St. Lawrence and North Shore from September 17, 2000 to October 6, 2001` purpose `the Sunday that begins the week referred to in subsection 10(1) of the Act` `my region` `my region's regional rate of unemployment under regulation 17(1)` `the neighbouring region's regional rate of unemployment under regulation 17(1)`
        `the answer under reg 17.1(9)` MEANS `reg 17.1(9) the applicable regional rate for a claimant outside Canada last employed in Lower St. Lawrence and North Shore from September 17, 2000 to October 6, 2001` purpose `the Sunday that begins the week referred to in subsection 10(1) of the Act` `my region` `my region's regional rate of unemployment under regulation 17(1)` `the neighbouring region's regional rate of unemployment under regulation 17(1)`
        `the answer under reg 17.1(10)` MEANS `reg 17.1(10) the applicable regional rate for a claimant resident in Lower St. Lawrence and North Shore from October 7, 2001 to October 12, 2002` purpose `the Sunday that begins the week referred to in subsection 10(1) of the Act` `my region` `my region's regional rate of unemployment under regulation 17(1)` `the neighbouring region's regional rate of unemployment under regulation 17(1)`
        `the answer under reg 17.1(11)` MEANS `reg 17.1(11) the applicable regional rate for a claimant outside Canada last employed in Lower St. Lawrence and North Shore from October 7, 2001 to October 12, 2002` purpose `the Sunday that begins the week referred to in subsection 10(1) of the Act` `my region` `my region's regional rate of unemployment under regulation 17(1)` `the neighbouring region's regional rate of unemployment under regulation 17(1)`
        `the answer under reg 17.1(12)` MEANS `reg 17.1(12) the applicable regional rate for a claimant resident in Lower St. Lawrence and North Shore from October 13, 2002 to April 7, 2012` purpose `the Sunday that begins the week referred to in subsection 10(1) of the Act` `my region` `my region's regional rate of unemployment under regulation 17(1)` `the neighbouring region's regional rate of unemployment under regulation 17(1)` `the day the special rates cease`
        `the answer under reg 17.1(13)` MEANS `reg 17.1(13) the applicable regional rate for a claimant outside Canada last employed in Lower St. Lawrence and North Shore from October 13, 2002 to April 7, 2012` purpose `the Sunday that begins the week referred to in subsection 10(1) of the Act` `my region` `my region's regional rate of unemployment under regulation 17(1)` `the neighbouring region's regional rate of unemployment under regulation 17(1)` `the day the special rates cease`

@export Has the Commission published the notice that a special regional rate of unemployment has stopped having effect, under regulation 17.1(18)?
GIVEN `the condition in subsection 17.1(16) or (17) has been satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the condition in subsection 17.1(16) or (17) been satisfied (the hours and weeks for your region are exactly the same using the special rate as using the ordinary rate)?
      `the Commission published a notice in the Canada Gazette that specifies the provisions that cease to have effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Commission publish a notice in the Canada Gazette that specifies the provisions that cease to have effect?
      `the Commission also published the notice on its website` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Commission also publish the notice on its website?
      `the notice was published as soon as possible after the condition was satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice published as soon as possible after the condition was satisfied?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the Commission published the notice that a special regional rate of unemployment has stopped having effect, under regulation 17.1(18)` IF
    `reg 17.1(18) the Commission has published the notice as required`
        `the condition in subsection 17.1(16) or (17) has been satisfied`
        `the Commission published a notice in the Canada Gazette that specifies the provisions that cease to have effect`
        `the Commission also published the notice on its website`
        `the notice was published as soon as possible after the condition was satisfied`
